proof.text:
For R to S to T and any T-complex M, precompose the proposed composite with eta_{T,M}. Using step 4 twice gives
((sigma_{R,S} r_{S,T}) sigma_{S,T})_{Q_TM} eta_{T,M}
= sigma_{R,S,Q_S C(r_{S,T})M} eta_{S,C(r_{S,T})M}
= eta_{R,C(r_{R,S})C(r_{S,T})M}
= eta_{R,C(r_{R,T})M}.
Thus the composite and sigma_{R,T} have the same image in the universal bijection for H_T with target H_R r_{R,T}; injectivity proves their equality as natural transformations. Similarly id_{H_R} precomposed with eta_R is eta_R, so uniqueness gives sigma_{R,R}=id_{H_R}. These are equalities of the already natural derived transformations. All arguments used exactness of restriction and the ringed-topos composition theorem, never flatness of a ring map or preservation of injectives by restriction.
